abstract: >-
  Code, per-question result files and reproduction commands for a measurement study of
  evidence localisation inside the gold document in retrieval-augmented generation
  evaluation on QASPER and Natural Questions: seven localisers (BM25, four dense
  bi-encoders, two cross-encoder rerankers) under one protocol with an analytic,
  length-aware chance level; Holm-corrected paired tests and a document-level cluster
  bootstrap; union and rank-correlation analyses; admission-budget and chunk-size sweeps;
  and the scripts behind a human-reviewed failure-attribution study and a gold-span
  completeness adjudication, whose labels and estimates are in results/goldspan_adjudication.
  Version 1.1.0 is a Git tag and is not deposited on Zenodo, so it has no DOI of its own.
  The archived code release is v1.0.0 (doi:10.5281/zenodo.22879358); the human annotation
  package is a separate version of the same Zenodo record (doi:10.5281/zenodo.22879569).
  The record's concept DOI, 10.5281/zenodo.22879357, resolves to its latest version,
  currently the annotation package, and DataCite registers it as a CC BY 4.0 dataset, so
  it is not a DOI for the code. The manuscript "Right document, wrong passage: evidence
  localisation in retrieval-augmented generation evaluation on QASPER and Natural
  Questions" was submitted to Language Resources and Evaluation on 23 September 2026 and
  is not yet peer-reviewed, accepted or published; cite this software release until it is.
